G4128.b:
⟪πλῆθος⟫, -ους, τό,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨רֹב⁩, also for ⁨הָמוֹן⁩, etc.;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪a great number⟫, ⟪a multitude⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of things: ἰχθύων, ⟦Luke 5:6|Lk 5:6⟧, ⟦John 21:6|Jo 21:6⟧; φρυγάνων, ⟦Acts 28:3|Ac 28:3⟧; ἁμαρτιιῶν, ⟦James 5:20|Ja 5:20⟧, ⟦1 Peter 4:8|I Pe 4:8⟧; τ. πλήθει, ⟪in multitude⟫, ⟦Hebrews 11:12|He 11:12⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of persons: ⟦Acts 21:22|Ac 21:22⟧ (WH, R, om.); c. gen., ⟦Luke 2:13|Lk 2:13⟧, ⟦John 5:3|Jo 5:3⟧, ⟦Acts 5:14|Ac 5:14⟧; π. πολύ (πολὺ π.), ⟦Mark 3:7|Mk 3:7⟧, ⟦Mark 3:8|8⟧; id. c. gen., ⟦Luke 6:17|Lk 6:17⟧ ⟦Luke 23:27|23:27⟧, ⟦Acts 14:1|Ac 14:1⟧ ⟦Acts 17:4|17:4⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of persons, c. art., ⟪the whole number⟫, ⟪the multitude⟫ (in Plat., Thuc., Xen., al., = δῆμος, the commons, or-opp. to δῆμος-the populace): ⟦Acts 2:6|Ac 2:6⟧ ⟦Acts 15:30|15:30⟧ ⟦Acts 19:9|19:9⟧ ⟦Acts 23:7|23:7⟧; τ. λαοῦ, ⟦Acts 21:36|Ac 21:36⟧; τ. πόλεως, ⟦Acts 14:4|Ac 14:4⟧; πᾶν τὸ π., ⟦Acts 15:12|Ac 15:12⟧; c. gen., ⟦Luke 1:10|Lk 1:10⟧ ⟦Luke 8:37|8:37⟧ ⟦Luke 19:37|19:37⟧ ⟦Luke 23:1|23:1⟧, ⟦Acts 4:32|Ac 4:32⟧ ⟦Acts 5:16|5:16⟧ ⟦Acts 6:2|6:2⟧, ⟦Acts 6:5|5⟧ ⟦Acts 25:24|25:24⟧.†

G4137.b:
⟪πληρόω⟫, -ῶ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨מָלֵא⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to fill⟫, ⟪make full⟫, ⟪fill to the full⟫, c. acc.;
	⟪(a)⟫ of things: pass. (σαψήνη, φάραγξ), ⟦Matthew 13:48|Mt 13:48⟧, ⟦Luke 3:5|Lk 3:5⟧(LXX); fig., ⟦Matthew 23:32|Mt 23:32⟧; but chiefly of immaterial things: πᾶσαν χρείαν, ⟦Philippians 4:19|Phl 4:19⟧; ἦχος ἐπλήρωσε τ. οἶκον, ⟦Acts 2:2|Ac 2:2⟧; c. gen. rei (cl.), ⟦Acts 5:28|Ac 5:28⟧; pass., seq. ἐκ, ⟦John 12:3|Jo 12:3⟧ (cf. B1., § 36, 4); π. τ. καρδίαν, ⟦John 16:6|Jo 16:6⟧, ⟦Acts 5:3|Ac 5:3⟧; metaph., of the all-pervading activity of Christ, ⟦Ephesians 4:10|Eph 4:10⟧; mid., ⟦Ephesians 1:23|Eph 1:23⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of persons: ⟪to fill⟫ with, ⟪cause to abound⟫ in: c. gen. rei (cl.), ⟦Acts 2:28|Ac 2:28⟧(LXX), ⟦Romans 15:13|Ro 15:13⟧; pass., ⟪to be filled⟫ with, ⟪abound⟫ in: ⟦Ephesians 3:19|Eph 3:19⟧, ⟦Philippians 4:18|Phl 4:18⟧; c. gen. rei (cl.), ⟦Acts 13:52|Ac 13:52⟧, ⟦Romans 15:14|Ro 15:14⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:4|II Ti 1:4⟧; c. dat. (Æsch., al.), ⟦Luke 2:40|Lk 2:40⟧ (c. gen., T), ⟦Romans 1:29|Ro 1:29⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 7:4|II Co 7:4⟧; c. acc. (so in π., v. MM, xx), ⟦Philippians 1:11|Phl 1:11⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:9|Col 1:9⟧; seq. ἐν, ⟦Ephesians 5:18|Eph 5:18⟧, ⟦Colossians 2:10|Col 2:10⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to complete⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to complete⟫, ⟪fulfil⟫: of number, ⟦Revelation 6:11|Re 6:11⟧, WH, txt.; of time (MM, xx), ⟦Mark 1:15|Mk 1:15⟧, ⟦Luke 21:24|Lk 21:24⟧, ⟦John 7:8|Jo 7:8⟧, ⟦Acts 7:23|Ac 7:23⟧, ⟦Acts 7:30|30⟧ ⟦Acts 9:23|9:23⟧ ⟦Acts 24:27|24:27⟧; ἐυδοκίαν, ⟦2 Thessalonians 1:11|II Th 1:11⟧; τ. χαράν, ⟦Philippians 2:2|Phl 2:2⟧; pass., ⟦John 3:29|Jo 3:29⟧ ⟦John 15:11|15:11⟧ ⟦John 16:24|16:24⟧ ⟦John 17:13|17:13⟧, ⟦1 John 1:4|I Jo 1:4⟧, ⟦2 John 1:12|II Jo 12⟧; τ. ἔργα, ⟦Revelation 3:2|Re 3:2⟧; ἡ ὑπακοή, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:6|II Co 10:6⟧; τ. πάσχα, ⟦Luke 22:16|Lk 22:16⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to execute⟫, ⟪accomplish⟫, ⟪carry out to the full⟫: ⟦Matthew 3:15|Mt 3:15⟧, ⟦Luke 7:1|Lk 7:1⟧ ⟦Luke 9:31|9:31⟧, ⟦Acts 12:25|Ac 12:25⟧ ⟦Acts 13:25|13:25⟧ ⟦Acts 14:26|14:26⟧ ⟦Acts 19:21|19:21⟧, ⟦Romans 8:4|Ro 8:4⟧ ⟦Romans 13:8|13:8⟧ ⟦Romans 15:19|15:19⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:14|Ga 5:14⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:25|Col 1:25⟧ ⟦Colossians 4:17|4:17⟧, ⟦Revelation 6:11|Re 6:11⟧, T, WH, R, mg.;
	⟪(c)⟫ of sayings, prophecies, etc., ⟪to bring to pass⟫, ⟪fulfil⟫: ⟦Matthew 1:22|Mt 1:22⟧ ⟦Matthew 2:15|2:15⟧, ⟦Matthew 2:17|17⟧, ⟦Matthew 2:23|23⟧ ⟦Matthew 4:14|4:14⟧ ⟦Matthew 5:17|5:17⟧ ⟦Matthew 8:17|8:17⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:17|12:17⟧ ⟦Matthew 13:35|13:35⟧ ⟦Matthew 21:4|21:4⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:54|26:54⟧, ⟦Matthew 26:56|56⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:9|27:9⟧, ⟦Mark 14:49|Mk 14:49⟧ ⟦Mark 15:28|15:28⟧ (WH, R, txt. om.), ⟦Luke 1:20|Lk 1:20⟧ ⟦Luke 4:21|4:21⟧ ⟦Luke 24:44|24:44⟧, ⟦John 12:38|Jo 12:38⟧ ⟦John 13:18|13:18⟧ ⟦John 15:25|15:25⟧ ⟦John 17:12|17:12⟧ ⟦John 18:9|18:9⟧, ⟦John 18:32|32⟧ ⟦John 19:24|19:24⟧, ⟦John 19:36|36⟧, ⟦Acts 1:16|Ac 1:16⟧ ⟦Acts 3:18|3:18⟧ ⟦Acts 13:27|13:27⟧, ⟦James 2:23|Ja 2:23⟧ (cf. Lft., Col., 255 ff.).†

G4138.b:
⟪πλήρωμα⟫, -τος, τό
(< πληρόω), [in LXX for ⁨מְלֹא⁩;] the result of the action involved in πληρόω (Lft., Col., 255 ff.; AR, Eph., 255 ff.), hence,
⟪1.⟫ in passive sense, ⟪that which has been completed⟫, ⟪complement⟫, ⟪plenitude⟫, ⟪fullness⟫ (in Xen., Luc., Polyb., al., of a ship's crew or cargo, and by meton. of the ship itself): ⟦John 1:16|Jo 1:16⟧, ⟦Romans 11:12|Ro 11:12⟧, ⟦Romans 11:25|25⟧ ⟦Romans 15:29|15:29⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:26|I Co 10:26⟧(LXX), ⟦Ephesians 1:23|Eph 1:23⟧ (AR, 42 ff.) ⟦Ephesians 3:19|3:19⟧ (AR. 87 ff.) ⟦Ephesians 4:13|4:13⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:19|Col 1:19⟧ ⟦Colossians 2:9|2:9⟧; of time, ⟦Galatians 4:4|Ga 4:4⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:10|Eph 1:10⟧; κοφίνων (σφυρίδων) πληρώματα, ⟪basketfuls⟫, ⟦Mark 6:43|Mk 6:43⟧ ⟦Mark 8:20|8:20⟧.
⟪2.⟫ In active sense (= πλήρωσις, as freq. in words of these formations, cf. κτίσις, and v. MM, xx);
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪that which fills up⟫ (but v. Lft., Col., 255 ff.): ⟦Matthew 9:16|Mt 9:16⟧, ⟦Mark 2:21|Mk 2:21⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a filling up⟫, ⟪completing⟫, ⟪fulfilment⟫: ⟦Romans 13:10|Ro 13:10⟧.†

G4152.b:
* ⟪πνευματικός⟫, -ή, -όν
(< πνεῦμα),
⟪1.⟫ ⟪of⟫ or ⟪caused by the wind⟫, ⟪air⟫ or ⟪breath⟫ (Arist., al.).
⟪2.⟫ ⟪spiritual⟫ (opp. to σωματικός, Plut.);
	⟪(a)⟫ of created beings: τὰ π. (RV, the spiritual hosts), ⟦Ephesians 6:12|Eph 6:12⟧; of that which is related to the human spirit, opp. to ψυχικός, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:44|I Co 15:44⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:46|46⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of that which belongs to or is actuated by the Divine Spirit;
		⟪α⟫ of persons: ⟦1 Corinthians 2:15|I Co 2:15⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 3:1|3:1⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 14:37|14:37⟧, ⟦Galatians 6:1|Ga 6:1⟧; οἶκος π., fig., ⟦1 Peter 2:5|I Pe 2:5⟧;
		⟪β⟫ of things: ⟦Romans 1:11|Ro 1:11⟧ ⟦Romans 7:14|7:14⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:13|I Co 2:13⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 10:3|10:3⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:4|4⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 12:1|12:1⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 14:1|14:1⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:3|Eph 1:3⟧ ⟦Ephesians 5:19|5:19⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:9|Col 1:9⟧ ⟦Colossians 3:16|3:16⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:5|I Pe 2:5⟧; opp. to τ. σαρκικά, ⟦Romans 15:27|Ro 15:27⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:11|I Co 9:11⟧.†
SYN.: ψυχικός, q.v., and cf. DB, ii, 410, iv, 612.

G4153.b:
*† ⟪πνευματικῶς⟫, adv.
(< πνεῦμα), ⟪spiritually⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ by the aid of the Holy Spirit: ⟦1 Corinthians 2:13|I Co 2:13⟧(WH, mg.), ⟦1 Corinthians 2:14|14⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ in a spiritual sense: ⟦Revelation 11:8|Re 11:8⟧.†

G4159.b:
