⟪(b)⟫ in indirect questions = ὁποῖος: ⟦Matthew 21:24|Mt 21:24⟧, ⟦Matthew 21:27|27⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:43|24:43⟧, ⟦Mark 11:29|Mk 11:29⟧, ⟦Mark 11:33|33⟧, ⟦Luke 12:39|Lk 12:39⟧ ⟦Luke 20:2|20:2⟧, ⟦Luke 20:8|8⟧, ⟦John 12:33|Jo 12:33⟧ ⟦John 18:32|18:32⟧ ⟦John 21:19|21:19⟧, ⟦Acts 23:34|Ac 23:34⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:11|I Pe 1:11⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:3|Re 3:3⟧; ποίας (sc. ὁδοῦ), ⟦Luke 5:19|Lk 5:19⟧.†

G4190.b:
⟪πονηρός⟫, -ά, -όν
(< πονέω, to toil), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨רַע⁩;]
⟪1.⟫
	⟪(a)⟫ of persons, ⟪oppressed by toils⟫ (Hes.);
	⟪(b)⟫ of things, ⟪toilsome⟫, ⟪painful⟫ (καιρός, Si 51:12): ⟦Ephesians 5:16|Eph 5:16⟧ ⟦Ephesians 6:13|6:13⟧, ⟦Revelation 16:2|Re 16:2⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪bad⟫, ⟪worthless⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ in physical sense: καρπός, ⟦Matthew 7:17|Mt 7:17⟧, ⟦Matthew 7:18|18⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ in ethical sense, ⟪bad⟫, ⟪evil⟫, ⟪wicked⟫;
		⟪(α)⟫ of persons: ⟦Matthew 7:11|Mt 7:11⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:34|12:34⟧, ⟦Matthew 12:35|35⟧ ⟦Matthew 18:32|18:32⟧ ⟦Matthew 25:26|25:26⟧, ⟦Luke 6:45|Lk 6:45⟧ ⟦Luke 11:13|11:13⟧ ⟦Luke 19:22|19:22⟧, ⟦Acts 17:5|Ac 17:5⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 3:2|II Th 3:2⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 3:13|II Ti 3:13⟧; γενεά, ⟦Matthew 12:39|Mt 12:39⟧, ⟦Matthew 12:45|45⟧ ⟦Matthew 16:4|16:4⟧, ⟦Luke 11:29|Lk 11:29⟧; πνεῦμια, ⟦Matthew 12:45|Mt 12:45⟧, ⟦Luke 7:21|Lk 7:21⟧ ⟦Luke 8:2|8:2⟧ ⟦Luke 11:26|11:26⟧, ⟦Acts 19:12|Ac 19:12⟧, ⟦Acts 19:13|13⟧, ⟦Acts 19:15|15⟧, ⟦Acts 19:16|16⟧; as subst., οἱ π., opp. to δίκαιοι, ⟦Matthew 13:49|Mt 13:49⟧; to ἀγαθοί, ⟦Matthew 5:45|Mt 5:45⟧ ⟦Matthew 22:10|22:10⟧; οἱ ἀχάριστοι καὶ π., ⟦Luke 6:35|Lk 6:35⟧; sing., ὁ π., ⟦Matthew 5:39|Mt 5:39⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:13|I Co 5:13⟧; id. esp. of Satan, ⟪the evil one⟫, ⟦Matthew 5:37|Mt 5:37⟧ ⟦Matthew 6:13|6:13⟧ (v. Lft., Notes, 125 ff.; but cf. McN, in l.) ⟦Matthew 13:19|13:19⟧, ⟦Matthew 13:38|38⟧, ⟦Luke 11:4|Lk 11:4⟧ (WH, R, om.), ⟦John 17:15|Jo 17:15⟧, ⟦Ephesians 6:16|Eph 6:16⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 3:3|II Th 3:3⟧ (Lft., Notes, 125 ff.), ⟦1 John 2:13|I Jo 2:13⟧, ⟦1 John 2:14|14⟧ ⟦1 John 3:12|3:12⟧ ⟦1 John 5:18|5:18⟧, ⟦1 John 5:19|19⟧;
		⟪(β)⟫ of things: ⟦Matthew 5:11|Mt 5:11⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:35|12:35⟧ ⟦Matthew 15:19|15:19⟧, ⟦Luke 6:22|Lk 6:22⟧, ⟦Luke 6:45|45⟧, ⟦John 3:19|Jo 3:19⟧ ⟦John 7:7|7:7⟧, ⟦Acts 18:14|Ac 18:14⟧ ⟦Acts 25:18|25:18⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:4|Ga 1:4⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:21|Col 1:21⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 6:4|I Ti 6:4⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 4:18|II Ti 4:18⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:12|He 3:12⟧ ⟦Hebrews 10:22|10:22⟧, ⟦James 2:4|Ja 2:4⟧ ⟦James 4:16|4:16⟧, ⟦1 John 3:12|I Jo 3:12⟧, ⟦2 John 1:11|II Jo 11⟧, ⟦3 John 1:10|III Jo 10⟧; ὀφθαλμός (q.v.), ⟦Matthew 6:23|Mt 6:23⟧ ⟦Matthew 20:15|20:15⟧, ⟦Mark 7:22|Mk 7:22⟧, ⟦Luke 11:34|Lk 11:34⟧; as subst., neut., τὸ π., ⟦Acts 28:21|Ac 28:21⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:22|I Th 5:22⟧; opp. to ἀγαθόν, ⟦Luke 6:45|Lk 6:45⟧, ⟦Romans 12:9|Ro 12:9⟧; pl., ⟦Matthew 9:4|Mt 9:4⟧, ⟦Mark 7:23|Mk 7:23⟧, ⟦Luke 3:19|Lk 3:19⟧.†
SYN.: v.s. ἄθεσμος.

G4198.b:
⟪πορεύω⟫,
